Theorem CN-1: Dead iff Absent bidirectional canonicalization

  Preconditions:
    - s is an AimsState per the canonical proof notation
      sec-Per-Dimension-Symbol-Set
    - s.consumption in {Dead, Linear, Affine, Unrestricted}
    - s.cardinality in {Absent, Once, Many}
    - canonicalize_cn1 applies the bidirectional rule from Annex E §AIMS + sec-1 lattice consistency invariants

  Soundness property:
    Forall s in AimsState. canonicalize_cn1(s) yields (cons, card) where
    cons = Dead iff card = Absent.

  Proof obligation:
    Finite enumeration over 4 Consumption x 3 Cardinality = 12 input states.
    For each (cons, card), apply CN-1's bidirectional forcing rule:
      if cons = Dead OR card = Absent: yield (Dead, Absent)
      else: preserve (cons, card)
    Verify the Dead iff Absent invariant holds on all 12 canonical outputs.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (finite-state enumeration over the 12-state product
        per section_03::verify_cn1_dead_absent_bidirectional)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_03 case_analysis engine discharges CN-1 via 12-state finite enumeration over Consumption x Cardinality
